The Coven Mother is the elite class of the Coven Sage (neutral witch route).
It asks no alignment at level 30. Where other witches hold the foes they hit,
the Coven Mother holds the whole group: her hexes land more often, last
longer and cost less.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Coven's Will      hexes land 5 points more often (never above 90)
  35 Lasting hexes     hexes last a round longer (a foe is still never held
                       more than half a fight)
  40 Cheaper hexes     hexes cost 20% less mana
  45 Breaking the boss a boss resists her hexes by 12 instead of 25
  50 Twin Hex          every third hex she lands also leaves its target
                       exposed for 1 round
  55 Surer hexes       hexes land another 5 points more often
  60 Coven Circle      once a battle, the first hex that would be resisted
                       lands anyway (a boss still halves its length)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

She hexes on her own like any witch (<ansi fg="command">help witch</ansi>). Coven Circle says so when it turns a resist into a
hold.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Witch elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves, Iron Will, Hex Reach.
See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help witch-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
